From 788685ca59a371bb02f2f15c8a9da7ef08fa5b03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anshuman Singh <anshuman.s@npci.org.in>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:35:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(llm): resolve provider family from the registry,
 not the model's name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 0 of the model-agnostic work (docs/llm/model_agnostic_architecture_audit.md).
Six live defects, all one root cause: provider/family was inferred by parsing a
model's NAME, which stopped being sound once admins could register arbitrary
models through the "LLM Providers" screen. Each gets worse the moment
per-feature model assignment ships, so they land first and on their own.

Adds services/endpoint_model_catalog.family_of() — the registry-backed
predicate the three name-parsing sites now share. endpoint_model_catalog
already existed for exactly this ("rather than add a sixth predicate, this
module delegates to the AUTHORITATIVE source"), so this extends it instead of
adding a seventh.

- §3.10 provider/model mismatch: feedback_processor, classifier and
  hybrid_retriever (x2) hardcoded provider="claude" beside a dynamically
  resolved model. /llm/generate picks its gateway from `provider` alone and
  forwards `model` untouched, so repointing the "haiku" tier at another vendor
  sent a mismatched pair. They now derive the provider via the new
  proxy_provider_for() and skip the (optional) enrichment when no built-in
  gateway can serve the model, rather than guessing.

- §3.14 budget bypass: _is_inhouse_model was a seven-prefix deny-list with
  "not one of these => in-house => free => skip budget". Every paid model
  outside those prefixes was exempted from budget enforcement entirely —
  mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct, deepseek-chat, o3-mini, Bedrock
  us.anthropic.*, Vertex ...@20240620, every OpenRouter vendor/model id, and
  every router tier hint. Now delegates to classify_model, which fails closed.
  Also stops lower-casing the id: both halves of classify_model match exactly
  against a catalogue and real in-house ids carry capitals (gemma-4-31B-it),
  so lower-casing would newly bill a free in-house model.

- §3.15 AgentStudio misroute: _classify_model's "everything else is local"
  default sent OpenRouter ids like anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 to the in-house
  LiteLLM endpoint. Consults the registry first; prefixes remain as the offline
  fallback. Also drops a docstring reference to
  services/llm_proxy/main.py::_provider_from_model, which does not exist.

- §3.16 kill-switch gap: /llm/generate never checked BLOCKED_MODELS against
  the resolved model at all, so ENABLE_CLI_OPUS_5=false was refused on the
  gateway path and still served through the proxy. Adds the request-path guard
  (the authoritative fix) and ports the three missing switches into the proxy's
  registry copy as defence in depth. The proxy cannot import the root registry
  — main.py shadows `core` on sys.path deliberately — so a new
  release_checks.py check asserts the two copies stay in sync. The proxy's one
  ENABLE_OPUS branch also added CLAUDE_OPUS_46_MODEL where root adds
  CLAUDE_OPUS_48_MODEL, so Opus 4.8 was never blocked in the proxy at all.

- §3.17 blank-model guard: porting those switches puts "" into the proxy's
  BLOCKED_MODELS by default (a blank CLAUDE_OPUS_5_MODEL is added whenever
  ENABLE_CLI_OPUS_5 is off), which made the proxy's unguarded
  class-definition-time check raise at import — taking down every Claude model,
  not one. Adds the `CLAUDE_MODEL and` guard root has carried since the same
  outage. Verified both ways: without the guard the import raises, with it the
  module loads.

- §3.18 generate_with_model: validated `model` against BLOCKED_MODELS then
  called self.generate(prompt) without forwarding it, so the caller's model was
  silently replaced by the deployment default. Zero callers repo-wide and the
  name promises the opposite of what it does, so both copies are removed rather
  than fixed.

Two further defects found while verifying the above, same code paths:
/llm/generate returns application/x-ndjson, but feedback_processor and
hybrid_retriever's query decomposition called resp.json() on it. That raised
JSONDecodeError on every call, so prompt-improvement suggestions always
returned None and decomposition always returned []. Both now use a shared
llm_proxy_ndjson_text() helper in core/proxy_tool_use.py, alongside
llm_proxy_headers.

38 new tests in tests/core/ (which is in the default CI pytest paths, unlike
tests/models/). No new failures against scripts/ci/known_failures.txt; all
release checks pass, and the new parity check was negative-tested by reverting
a gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
